{"command": "sed -n 100,200p /testbed/specs/001-transactions/spec.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "True, False; attempt put with a bare string as tags, with a non-string tag\nentry, and with an uncopyable value; verify each raises the documented error\nand the prior state is intact.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** maxsize values 0, -1, 2.5, \"5\", True, False, **When**\nTaggedCache(maxsize) is called, **Then** a ValueError is raised (True and\nFalse are rejected even though they are integers).\n2. **Given** a cache with key k stored under tag \"a\", **When** put(k, v,\ntags=\"a\") (bare string) is called, **Then** ValueError is raised and get(k)\nstill returns the old value with tag \"a\" still active (invalidate(\"a\") would\nstill return 1).\n3. **Given** a cache with key k stored, **When** put(k, v, tags=(\"a\", 1)) is\ncalled, **Then** ValueError is raised and the old value/tags/recency are\nunchanged.\n4. **Given** a cache with key k stored, **When** put(k, value, tags) is called\nwith a value that cannot be deep-copied, **Then** an error is raised and the\nold value, tags, and recency position are unchanged.\n5. **Given** a cache of maxsize 2, **When** two entries (large nested objects\nand a small int) are stored, **Then** both fit and a third put evicts the LRU\nentry; size never affects slot cost.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- Tags given as a finite iterable (list, tuple, generator, set) of strings are\n  accepted; duplicate tags are deduplicated, so invalidate counts each live\n  entry once.\n- An empty tags iterable (including the default) stores the entry with no tag\n  memberships.\n- A bare string passed as tags is rejected (a string is an iterable of\n  characters, but it is not a valid tag collection).\n- A tag entry that is not a string is rejected.\n- Replacing an existing key with new tags removes the old tag memberships\n  before the new ones take effect (no transient double membership observable\n  through invalidate).\n- LRU eviction of a tagged entry removes its tag memberships so later reuse of\n  the same key starts clean.\n- get on a hit refreshes recency; get on a miss raises KeyError and changes\n  nothing.\n- len(cache) always equals the number of live entries (never exceeds maxsize,\n  never counts evicted or invalidated entries).\n- Keys are hashable; unhashable keys raise TypeError on put (standard Python\n  hashing contract).\n\n## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n**R01 - Storage and retrieval**\n\n- **FR-001**: TaggedCache MUST be constructible with a single required\n  maxsize argument.\n- **FR-002**: put(key, value, tags=()) MUST insert a new entry or replace an\n  existing one for the same key; keys MUST be hashable.\n- **FR-003**: get(key) MUST return a detached deep copy of the stored value;\n  mutating the returned object (including nested members) MUST NOT affect the\n  stored value.\n- **FR-004**: get(key) MUST raise KeyError when the key is not currently\n  stored.\n- **FR-005**: Values MUST be deep-copied on input, so later mutation of the\n  caller's original object MUST NOT change the stored content.\n- **FR-006**: tags MUST be a finite iterable of strings; duplicate tags MUST\n  be deduplicated so each live entry counts once per tag.\n- **FR-007**: A bare string passed as tags MUST be rejected with ValueError,\n  as MUST any tag entry that is not a string.\n- **FR-008**: Tag validation errors MUST be raised before any existing cache\n  state (values, tags, recency) is changed.\n\n**R02 - Invalidation and LRU behavior**\n\n- **FR-009**: invalidate(tag) MUST remove exactly the currently cached entries\n  carrying that tag and MUST return the number of entries removed.\n- **FR-010**: Replacing a key via put MUST remove its old tag memberships\n  before the new tags take effect.\n- **FR-011**: LRU eviction MUST remove the evicted entry's tag memberships so\n  no stale membership affects later reuse of the same key.\n- **FR-012**: get(key) on a hit MUST refresh that entry's LRU recency.\n- **FR-013**: len(cache) MUST return the number of live entries.\n\n**R03 - Configuration and atomicity**\n\n- **FR-014**: maxsize MUST be a positive integer; bool values (True, False)\n  MUST be rejected; invalid maxsize MUST raise ValueError.\n- **FR-015**: A put that fails validation (invalid tags) or fails to copy the\n  value MUST leave the previously stored value, its tags, and its recency\n  position unchanged.\n- **FR-016**: Every stored value MUST cost exactly one capacity slot\n  regardless of object size or shape.\n\n### Key Entities *(include if feature involves data)*\n\n- **Cache entry**: A live mapping from one hashable key to one stored value\n  plus the set of tags it carries; occupies exactly one of the maxsize slots.\n- **Tag**: A string label shared by any number of live entries; used only for\n  bulk invalidation. A tag's membership set always reflects live entries only.\n- **Recency order**: The LRU ordering over live entries, updated on put (new\n  or replaced) and on get hits; determines which entry is evicted when the\n  cache is full.\n"}